{"author":{"id":"1d5f412cdeafe9987ad9876b0995bf5032718543d34c038a50cdb41808e9874c"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788305137,"nonce":"JR+UV+WvcHjIi46gefiMtSmIDew=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOULVc1M8AAAABPPhlgQ","github-url":"https://github.com/kanya-approve/torram-ng/issues/20","origin":"github"},"title":"BEP 47 padding files are not recognised","message":"Modern torrents — hybrid v1/v2 torrents especially — insert padding files so that real files start on piece boundaries. These are conventionally named `.pad/\u003clength\u003e` and carry `attr` containing `p`.\n\nThe tool treats them as ordinary files: it looks for candidates matching their size and, in the recovery path, would create `.pad/1234` in the output.\n\nCorrect handling is to keep them in the global offset map, since they occupy bytes in the piece stream, but exclude them from the set of files to search for or write.","files":null}]}